  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Always write exactly four one-word choices. Never change the count or use a phrase as a choice.",
      "Exactly one choice matches the stem meaning. If two affixed words both fit, drop one of them.",
      "Use only Grade 2 affixes: un-, re-, pre-, dis-, mis-, -ful, -less, -ly, -er, -est, and -y.",
      "Do not use return as a re- target; kids hear it as go back, not again.",
      "Never pair dislike with unlike, or unread with reread as two keys for the same stem.",
      "Tier 1 distractors come from a different affix family and a different base word.",
      "Tier 2 distractors may share a base or a close affix, but only one word may fit.",
      "Tier 3 distractors are near misses: un- versus re- or pre- on the same base, or -ful versus -less.",
      "Choices are whole kid words from school, home, food, pets, play, family, or weather. No brands and no real names."
    ]
  },
